<!-- EVALUATION CRITERIA -->
<section class="section" style="background:#e7eeff;" aria-labelledby="eval-heading">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2 id="eval-heading">What makes legal AI actually work</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="eval-grid">
      <div class="card" style="text-align:center;">
        <div class="num-circle">1</div>
        <h3 style="font-weight:700; font-size:0.9375rem; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Accuracy and hallucination risk</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.8125rem; line-height:1.6;">A legal AI tool must cite verifiable sources. Fabricated citations have already caused real sanctions in court, this is not a hypothetical risk.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="text-align:center;">
        <div class="num-circle">2</div>
        <h3 style="font-weight:700; font-size:0.9375rem; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Confidentiality and privilege</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.8125rem; line-height:1.6;">Client documents can't flow through systems that retain or train on that data outside your engagement. Confidentiality has to be architected in, not assumed.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="text-align:center;">
        <div class="num-circle">3</div>
        <h3 style="font-weight:700; font-size:0.9375rem; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Jurisdiction-specific training</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.8125rem; line-height:1.6;">A tool trained on foreign case law produces confidently wrong answers in a UAE civil law context. Jurisdictional accuracy is not optional.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card" style="text-align:center;">
        <div class="num-circle">4</div>
        <h3 style="font-weight:700; font-size:0.9375rem; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Human review as final check</h3>
        <p style="color:#42474e; font-size:0.8125rem; line-height:1.6;">AI drafts and flags, but a lawyer decides. Any workflow that removes the final human review step is a professional risk, not a productivity win.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- INDUSTRY RESEARCH -->
<section class="section" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
