        <div>
          <p style="font-weight:700; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Time Allocation</p>
          <p style="color:#42474e; line-height:1.7;">Legal operations research consistently shows document review and administrative work consuming a disproportionate share of billable time relative to the strategic and advisory work clients actually value.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-weight:700; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Review Speed</p>
          <p style="color:#42474e; line-height:1.7;">Firms using AI-assisted contract review report first-pass review time drops of 50 to 90%, depending on contract complexity and how well the playbook is defined, freeing lawyers for negotiation and judgment calls.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p style="font-weight:700; color:#00253b; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Citation Risk</p>
          <p style="color:#42474e; line-height:1.7;">Multiple documented court cases involve lawyers sanctioned for submitting briefs with AI-fabricated citations. This is the clearest cautionary example in professional AI adoption, and the reason citation verification is non-negotiable in legal tooling.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
